  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` events now carry `amountCents` and `createdAt`, and `totalCents` and `placedAt` are still there. All 39 tests pass, and `npm run arch` reports no dependency violations.\n\n- **Values:** The new fields hold the same values as the old ones. `amountCents` equals `totalCents`, and `createdAt` equals `placedAt`.\n- **Schema version:** I left `schemaVersion` at 3, since adding fields doesn't break consumers that ignore unknown ones. If your consumers validate strictly or you version by field set, tell me and I'll bump it.\n- **Old names:** I marked `totalCents` and `placedAt` as deprecated in the doc comments. You can remove them in a later version once consumers have moved to the new names.\n- **Code changes:** The event type and builder are in `src/core/events.ts`. I updated the `deepEqual` assertion in `test/app.test.ts` to expect the new fields.\n- **HTTP responses:** I didn't touch the `POST /orders` response, which still uses `placedAt` and `totalCents`. I read your request as covering only the event. Say so if you want the HTTP response aligned too.",
